.TH WINEAPPX 1 "July 31, 2026" "@PACKAGE_STRING@" "Wine Programs"
.SH NAME
wineappx \- verify, unpack, deploy, query, and launch MSIX/AppX packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wineappx
.RI [ options ]
.B inspect
.I package
.br
.B wineappx
.RI [ options ]
.B unpack
.I package destination
.br
.B wineappx
.RI [ options ]
.BR initialize | list | recover | gc
.br
.B wineappx
.RI [ options ]
.BR install | update
.I package
.br
.B wineappx
.RI [ options ]
.BR remove | query
.I package_full_name
.br
.B wineappx
.RI [ options ]
.B launch
.I package_full_name application_id
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wineappx
is a command-line client for Wine's private MSIX/AppX package service.
It provides bounded, signed package inspection and extraction, transactional
deployment-store operations, catalog queries, and full-trust application
launch.
.PP
Inspection and extraction accept signed MSIX/AppX packages and signed
MSIX/AppX bundles.  Before any payload is extracted, the service verifies the
CMS signature and certificate chain, signed archive digests, block map,
per-block hashes, CRC and compression framing, manifest identity, content
types, and package layout.  The input file is opened without following a leaf
reparse point.
.PP
The current bundle policy selects only one neutral or target-architecture
application payload.  Bundles containing resource payloads, optional payloads,
encrypted payloads, unsupported payload types or architectures, or unsupported
qualifiers are rejected with exit status 1.  A bundle with no compatible
application payload or an ambiguous best payload is also rejected.
Installation and update accept both package files and bundles under the same
policy.  Every embedded package is verified before the selected payload is
published to the deployment store.
.PP
.B unpack
requires a destination which does not exist.  It canonicalizes the destination
to a drive-absolute Windows path, opens and retains every existing parent
without following reparse points or permitting deletion while the leaf is
created, and passes an exclusive handle for the new empty directory to the
extractor.  A failed extraction attempts to remove the new directory if it is
empty and reports any partial directory which must be discarded.
.SH COMMANDS
.IP "\fBinspect \fIpackage\fR"
Verify a package or bundle and print its identity, selection, applications,
dependencies, content identity, signer identity, and support status.
.IP "\fBunpack \fIpackage destination\fR"
Verify and extract a package, or the selected application payload of a bundle,
into a new directory.
.IP \fBinitialize\fR
Create a deployment store or validate an existing one.
.IP "\fBinstall \fIpackage\fR"
Install a new package or supported app-only bundle family generation.
.IP "\fBupdate \fIpackage\fR"
Update an installed package family.  Downgrades require
.BR --allow-downgrade .
.IP "\fBremove \fIpackage_full_name\fR"
Remove one exact installed package generation.  Active dependents and package
leases prevent unsafe removal.
.IP "\fBquery \fIpackage_full_name\fR"
Query one exact installed package.
.IP \fBlist\fR
List all installed packages and their full-trust applications.
.IP "\fBlaunch \fIpackage_full_name application_id\fR"
Build the validated package graph, retain generation leases, and launch one
declared full-trust application.
.IP \fBrecover\fR
Recover bounded interrupted deployment transactions.
.IP \fBgc\fR
Collect a bounded set of unpublished generations.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP "\fB--store \fIpath\fR"
Use the specified drive-absolute deployment store.  The default is
\fBC:\\Program Files\\WindowsApps\\.wine-msix-store\fR.
.IP "\fB--arch \fIarchitecture\fR"
Select \fBneutral\fR, \fBx86\fR, \fBx64\fR, \fBarm\fR, \fBarm64\fR, or
\fBx86a64\fR.  The default is the native processor architecture.
.IP \fB--allow-downgrade\fR
Allow a lower-version update.  This option is rejected for other commands.
.IP \fB--accept-weak-durability\fR
Accept a host filesystem which cannot flush directory metadata.  The result
remains atomically visible but may not survive sudden power loss.  Strict
durability is the default for deployment operations.
.IP "\fB--max-archive \fIbytes\fR"
Limit the archive size.  The default is 32 GiB and the maximum is 128 GiB.
.IP "\fB--max-expanded \fIbytes\fR"
Limit total expanded payload bytes and the deployment package quota.  The
default is 16 GiB and the maximum is 64 GiB.
.IP "\fB--free-space-floor \fIbytes\fR"
Require this many bytes to remain free.  The default is 2 GiB.
.IP \fB--wait\fR
Wait for the application started by
.B launch
and return its exit status.  This option is rejected for other commands.
.IP \fB\-h\fR,\fB\ \-\-help\fR
Show command help.
.PP
Byte limits are positive decimal integers with an optional binary
\fBK\fR, \fBM\fR, \fBG\fR, or \fBT\fR suffix.  \fBKiB\fR-style suffixes are
also accepted.  Options must precede the command; use \fB--\fR to end option
processing explicitly.
.SH OUTPUT
Successful commands write a stable, line-oriented
.B key=value
schema to standard output.  Numeric values are decimal unless prefixed by
\fB0x\fR.  Digests are lowercase hexadecimal.  Repeated records use zero-based
bracketed indices, for example
\fBpackage[0].application[1].id\fR.  String values escape backslash as
\fB\\\\\fR and the control characters tab, carriage return, and line feed as
\fB\\t\fR, \fB\\r\fR, and \fB\\n\fR.  Other control code units use
\fB\\uNNNN\fR.  A parser should split each record at the first equals sign and
then unescape the value.  Human-readable diagnostics are written only to
standard error.
.PP
.B inspect
starts with \fBcontainer=package\fR or \fBcontainer=bundle\fR and emits package
identity, version, architecture, verification-derived content and signer
identities, application and dependency records, and unsupported-reason
records.  Bundle output additionally identifies the selected inner package.
.PP
.B unpack
emits \fBextracted\fR and \fBdurability\fR.
Deployment mutations emit the affected package name when applicable, catalog
epoch, result flags, reclaimed entry and byte counts, and durability.
.B list
and
.B query
emit catalog epoch, package count, package records, and application records.
.B launch
emits the process identifier and, with \fB--wait\fR, the process exit status.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.IP 0
The command completed successfully.
.IP 1
Input verification, extraction, deployment, query, launch, or waiting failed.
.IP 2
The command line, option value, or operand count was invalid.
.IP 3
The required private appxsvc API set was unavailable.
.PP
With
.BR "launch --wait" ,
the launched application's exit status is returned instead of the values
above; \fBprocess_exit_code\fR records the same value on standard output.
.SH BUGS
Bugs can be reported on the
.UR https://bugs.winehq.org
.B Wine bug tracker
.UE .
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B wineappx
is part of the Wine distribution, which is available through WineHQ,
the
.UR https://www.winehq.org/
.B Wine development headquarters
.UE .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR wine (1),
.BR winepath (1)
